      "math_academy_id": "q-140444",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{5}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{30}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{6\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{30}})≈{83.01}^{∘}.\n$$",
